+The package is disposable after a verified launch: a consumer project ignores it
+rather than tracking it, and launch does not untrack files that are already in the
+project's history. The harness's own canonical repository is the exception — there
+the toolkit is the tracked source of truth. Installed project outputs are permanent
+project artifacts and remain separate from the toolkit either way.
+
+Bootstrap operation records live under `state/` in the package: launch answers, plans,
+receipts and dated reports. Deployment mappings, synchronization state and new patch
+bundles stay project-owned under `.harness/`. Preserve both when refreshing the toolkit,
+and exclude `state/` from portable releases. Project `.harness/launch/` and
+`.harness/state/` records from earlier versions are migration inputs, not the
+destination for new writes.
 
